# Blog Image Formatter

## Step 1 Convert to md file and extract the images

Inside the pixi environment, run the following command:

```bash
jupyter nbconvert --to markdown <FILE_NAME>.ipynb
```

## Transformation

When processing markdown blog posts, replace all markdown image references with centered HTML image tags.

On the images:

`![png](<PATH>)` and `![svg](<PATH>)` become:

```html
<center>
  <img src="/images/<PATH>" style="width: 900px;"/>
</center>
```

The `<PATH>` follows the pattern `<BLOG_NAME>_files/<IMAGE_NAME>.png` or `<BLOG_NAME>_files/<IMAGE_NAME>.svg`.

## Example

Before:

```markdown
![png](bayesian_power_ab_testing_files/bayesian_power_ab_testing_5_0.png)
```

After:

```html
<center>
  <img src="/images/bayesian_power_ab_testing_files/bayesian_power_ab_testing_5_0.png" style="width: 900px;"/>
</center>
```

Apply this to every `![png](...)` and `![svg](...)` occurrence in the file.

# Tables

Add <center> (and end </center>) to the beginning and end of the tables.

# Items

Make sure the lists are separated by a blank line.

## Example

Before:

- Item 1
- Item 2
- Item 3


After: 
 
- Item 1

- Item 2

- Item 3

